=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte","html_url":"https://github.com/unbyte","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-09-16T14:53:57Z","updated_at":"2020-09-16T15:14:34Z","body":"As a supplement to what @HcySunYang pointed out, calling some methods can both trigger and track in one effect, which can lead to an infinite recursion in some scenarios. \r\n\r\ne.g. `Array.prototype.push`, gets `.length` and sets values,\r\n\r\n```js\r\n  const a = reactive([])\r\n\r\n  const b = ref(0)\r\n  const c = ref(0)\r\n\r\n  watchEffect(() => {\r\n    if (b < 10)\r\n      a.push(1)\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  watchEffect(() => {\r\n    if (c > -10)\r\n      a.push(1)\r\n  })\r\n```\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/693460094/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"unbyte","id":5772358,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzIzNTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5772358?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte","html_url":"https://github.com/unbyte","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unbyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unby